  "explanation": {
    "md_es": [
      "**Pedir:** *I'd like a coffee, please.* o *Can I have a coffee, please?*",
      "",
      "**I'd like** = *I would like* (quisiera). Es más educado que *I want* (quiero), que suena brusco.",
      "",
      "**Siempre con *please*.**",
      "",
      "**Camarero:** *What would you like? · Anything else?*",
      "",
      "**Pagar:** *Here you are.* · *That's six pounds.* · *Thank you!*"
    ],
    "common_mistakes_es": [
      {
        "wrong": "I want a coffee.",
        "right": "I'd like a coffee, please.",
        "note": "I want suena brusco al pedir."
      },
      {
        "wrong": "Give me water.",
        "right": "Can I have some water, please?",
        "note": "Give me es una orden; mejor pedir con Can I have…?"
      }
    ],
